  "predicate": {
    "id": "uireq-030_original_clause_and_scenarios",
    "description": "WHEN arithmetic lowering selects a word layout, it SHALL expose named full-result components with the exact checked UInt128 semantic wrapper.",
    "domain": "Public32/64-bit little-endian typed components and actual selected B-owner Scalar Add/Sub/Mul lowering through run_draft_host_with_word_layout. Named full results retain carry/borrow and the complete256-bit product before exact checked UInt128/error10 selection. Generic implementation independently inspected; three normal and three error10 tests passed across both layouts, with17 original component observations retained.",
    "applicableEvidenceClasses": [
      "source",
      "scoped-observation",
      "declared-component-correspondence"
    ],
    "nativeRequiredByOriginal": false,
    "allOriginalScenarios": "WHEN arithmetic lowering selects a word layout, it SHALL expose named full-result components with the exact checked UInt128 semantic wrapper.\n\n#### Scenario: Carry, borrow and full product\n- **WHEN** b is 32 or 64 and checkedU128Add/Sub/Mul use little-endian limbs.\n- **THEN** addCarry_b(a,bv,carryIn) returns named {low,carryOut}, subBorrow_b(a,bv,borrowIn) returns {low,borrowOut}, and mulWide_b(a,bv) returns {low,high}; carry/borrow bits and multiply-accumulate whole-word carries have distinct types. The wrappers retain K mathematical-result/error10 meaning, including the full up-to-256-bit product before checked UInt128 selection. Independently specified normal results are (2^32−3)+8 = 2^32+5, (2^64+9)−7 = 2^64+2, and (2^48+1)·3 = 3·2^48+3; no layout or row-cost winner is selected."
  },
